p_04). Node 6262's only neighbours are {5896, 7040, 7712} (step_05), so the *unique* static route from 4061 to 6262 is 4061\u21927536\u21927549\u2192252\u21927712\u21926262.\n\n**Timing (600-unit bins, steps 06\u201311 + confirmations 12\u201316):**\n\n| hop | bin containing the single event |\n|---|---|\n| 4061\u21927536 | [26782, 27381] (steps 06/07/13) |\n| 7536\u21927549 | [26182, 26781] (steps 07/08/12) |\n| 7549\u2192252 | [27982, 28581] (steps 08/09/14) |\n| 252\u21927712 | [27382, 27981] (steps 09/10/15) |\n| 7712\u21926262 | [27382, 27981] (steps 10/11/16) |\n\nThe chain is **anti-chronological at two joints**. 7536 relayed to 7549 in bin [26182,26781], strictly *before* it was ever contacted by 4061 in [26782,27381] \u2014 the bins are disjoint, so no ordering ambiguity. Likewise 252\u21927712 precedes 7549\u2192252. Since the path is unique (4061 has one partner; 7536 has only two partners), there is no alternative branch to rescue ordering, and no 600-unit-delay chain can exist.\n\n**Confounder controls.** The window is busy (5,469 events, 4,946 active nodes, step_01), and 6262/7712 are locally active in the late window \u2014 but that volume/popularity is irrelevant: 4061 fires exactly once (step_02), and the one edge it emits arrives too late to feed the downstream relays.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_e2469334\",\n  \"decision\": \"absent\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"cascade\",\n  \"entities\": [4061, 7536, 7549, 252, 7712, 6262],\n  \"window\": [22582, 32182],\n  \"confidence\": 0.88,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_04\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_05\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_06\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_07\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_08\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_09\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_10\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_11\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_12\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_13\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_14\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_15\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_16\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_01\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"A static path 4061->7536->7549->252->7712->6262 exists and is unique, but it is not time-respecting: 7536 forwarded to 7549 in bin [26182,26781], strictly before 4061 ever contacted 7536 (bin [26782,27381]), and 252->7712 likewise precedes 7549->252. With 4061 emitting only one event and 7536 having only two partners, no alternate branch exists, so no chain of <=600-unit-delay steps can carry influence from 4061 to 6262. High background activity in the window does not supply such a chain.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 23749, "total_output_tokens": 7302, "total_tokens": 31051, "total_latency_ms": 91307, "llm_calls": 5, "schema_repairs": 0, "tool_protocol_errors": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}